-- title:
--   Finitely many vertex orbits for the even level-ℓ group
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and local data: a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero with uniformiser $\pi$, residue field of cardinality $r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, fraction field $K_0$; a domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$, $\pi$-adically complete with $(\pi)$ maximal, integral over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, with residually algebraically closed reduction, together with an $\mathcal O$-automorphism $F_r$ lifting the $r$-power map modulo $\pi$; and a homomorphism $v_{\det}:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by $\det g=u\pi^{n}$, $u\in\mathcal O^\times$, iff $v_{\det}(g)=n$. Fix further a prime $\bar r\neq r$ and $N\geq 1$ with $r\nmid N$; rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $a_1,b_1<0$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes\mathbb Q_w$ is a division algebra exactly at the place $w$ containing $\bar r$; an Eichler order $R_1$, that is $R_1=\Lambda_1'\cap\Lambda_2'$ for maximal orders with $[\Lambda_1':R_1]=N$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$; the place $v$ above $r$; the group $\tilde\Gamma=\Gamma t$ of units lying, at every place $w\neq v$, in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$; the homomorphism $\rho_0$ sending $g$ to the class of $\iota_0(g)$ in $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$; the even part $\tilde\Gamma'$ of $\tilde\Gamma$, cut out by $v_{\det}(\iota_0(x))$ even; a family $s$ of units and an adelic family $sf$ indexed by the primes $\ell\neq r,\bar r$, subject to hypotheses saying that $sf_\ell$ localises to $s_\ell$ away from $r$ and to $1$ at $r$, that the diagonal image of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}$ of $\Lambda_1$ at $R_1\cap R_1^{n_1}$ if $\ell\mid N$ and in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}$ of $R_1\cap R_1^{n_1}$ otherwise, and that $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$ (summarised here); and $\tilde\Gamma(\ell)=\tilde\Gamma\cap s_\ell\tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$. Then for each such $\ell$ there is a finite set $S$ of vertices of the lattice tree of $\mathcal O$ in $K_0$ (homothety classes of full lattices) such that every vertex $w$ satisfies $x\cdot w\in S$ for some $x$ in the image of $\tilde\Gamma'\cap\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$ under $\rho_0$.
--
--   This is the cocompactness input for the quaternionic uniformisation at $r$: the even away-from-$r$ unit group of an Eichler order, cut down by the level-raising congruence condition at a tower prime $\ell$, still acts on the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ with finitely many vertex orbits. It feeds the recognition of the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower as a fine moduli space, cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.forall_exists_eq_tower_of_geometricallyConnected_of_isOpen_of_nonempty_of_isUnit_two_of_isUnit_three`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.forall_exists_eq_tower_of_geometricallyConnected_of_isOpen_of_nonempty_of_isUnit_two_of_isUnit_three).
